WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.560
Okay, let's go to the phones at six one seven
eight three zero.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.050
Forty seven fifty and see what is on people's
minds.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:09.050
Oh.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:14.460
Let's go to Brody from Dallas, our friend
Brody from Dallas, who has written the guide

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.000
on how to call into the show.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.689
What's going on, Brody?

00:00:17.689 --> 00:00:22.159
Hey, David, I'm pretty good, how are you doing?

00:00:22.159 --> 00:00:23.159
Good.

00:00:23.159 --> 00:00:24.159
Awesome.

00:00:24.159 --> 00:00:28.669
Hey, so I know that Bernie Sanders has asked
his supporters as.

00:00:28.669 --> 00:00:36.720
Have you spoken on your show about the proper
direction in which to go as far as getting

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.400
our police more accountable?

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.400
Yes.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.710
Are we safer and doing it in the right way?

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:47.870
The question I have for you today is when
people who see that say that, look, we've

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:54.250
tried voting, we've tried activism, we've
tried legislative mechanisms, we've tried

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:56.220
judicial mechanisms.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:57.650
And now that's worked.

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:00.530
When people who come to you and say, hey,
David.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:06.979
I think that using a mechanism like a ballot
initiative or defunding to force people to

00:01:06.979 --> 00:01:12.729
come to the table to negotiate for a different
type of police department is the way to go.

00:01:12.729 --> 00:01:14.750
What would your response be to that?

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:20.329
Well, I would reject on principle this idea
of we've tried it.

00:01:20.329 --> 00:01:21.439
There has not been.

00:01:21.439 --> 00:01:26.189
I mean, listen, when you're talking about
police departments, this has to do primarily

00:01:26.189 --> 00:01:27.469
with with three things.

00:01:27.469 --> 00:01:34.640
It has to do with police chiefs who are in
most places appointed by mayors.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:40.859
So where have been the big movements to hold
mayors accountable for who has been selected

00:01:40.859 --> 00:01:41.859
as police chief?

00:01:41.859 --> 00:01:47.470
I mean, I'm sure we can find some examples,
but there's been no major movement to say,

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:53.659
elect, let's put in place the right mayors,
make police chiefs selection and police policy

00:01:53.659 --> 00:01:55.689
a huge part of those mayoral campaigns.

00:01:55.689 --> 00:02:00.390
I've been involved from the media side in
a bunch of different mayoral races, and it's

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:02.929
just it's just never been a thing.

00:02:02.929 --> 00:02:07.579
So then you've also got to look at governors
because a lot of funding for police is state

00:02:07.579 --> 00:02:10.690
funding for both state and local police.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:15.350
We finally heard from Andrew Cuomo with some
ultimatums when it when it comes to police.

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:18.970
But I would just reject the idea that we've,
quote, tried it.

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:25.780
Now, if we reject the idea that we have tried
it, would that mean that if there is a ballot

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:30.700
initiative or a push for a ballot initiative,
such as one that, for example, is coming up

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:39.150
where I am and the area in Fort Worth to restrict
a portion of the funding that goes to SWAT

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:40.450
and things like that?

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:44.410
Would you support a bet that ballot initiative
which is on the ballot?

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:46.820
And I don't mean would you support it one
way or the other?

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:48.870
Would you support letting voters have a say?

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:49.870
Oh, yeah, of course.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:54.120
I mean, so there is a question as to whether
you want to vote on civil rights.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.120
Right.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:59.540
So when we talk about, hey, should gay marriage
be legal, I am skeptical about letting people

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.130
vote on those things.

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:05.960
And people have voted the wrong way when it
comes to how tax money should be used.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:10.480
I am very much, as a general rule in favor
of letting the people have a say.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:15.160
So while I don't think defund the police is
the solution.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:19.430
If the public has said we want this on the
ballot, then of course that that it should

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:21.210
be on the ballot.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:22.530
Absolutely.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:26.160
Are there any other mechanisms that you would
suggest in terms of besides looking at governors

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:31.430
and who makes these appointments that people
can look at in terms of making a direct and

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:32.830
positive change in their community?

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:35.000
Yeah, I mean, I think it's getting involved.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:41.130
So when you talk about lobbying city councilors,
I mean, a lot a lot of people do we have to

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:48.940
turn the Internet activism into actually getting
involved in a in a local way because the national

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.990
movement around this is great for energy.

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:55.750
But the national movement is not going to
make, you know, the Back Bay neighborhood

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:59.860
of Boston necessarily demand or achieve change.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:03.560
So I think it's we've got to translate that
in the same way that like we've got to turn

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:07.350
the protests that started when Trump was elected
into voting in November.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:12.400
If we want to turn it into something, we have
to take these protests and turn it into a

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:16.190
very, very specific and calculated local activism.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.190
Awesome.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:23.370
Hey, I hopefully I lived up to the guy that
I created for calling in and I appreciate

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.690
the information and I love the show, man.

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:27.480
Keep it up and things from I work it.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:29.210
All right, Brody, great to hear from you.

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:30.530
Always great to hear from Brody.

